WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.760
- [Narrator] Cross-gender
dancing is when the roles

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.960
of both the female and
male are played by one man.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.860
Using costumes, masks and movement,

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.250
the dancers are able to easily transition

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:37.900
between the two-gendered
characters they are playing.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:46.990
In the past, males would play female roles

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:50.090
in performances and plays and
although women are now allowed

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:52.700
to perform, through those old rules,

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.363
this new dance was born.

00:01:19.906 --> 00:01:22.200
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.030
The dance moves themselves are mostly

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.930
traditional Indonesian styles.

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:28.710
Didik takes time
perfecting female movement

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:31.893
so his transitions can appear
as authentic as possible.

00:02:06.872 --> 00:02:09.390
Today, Didik travels the
world teaching people

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:12.060
about this form of dance,
preserving the culture

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.820
and tradition for future generations.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.230
And in doing so, he's making a difference

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:19.733
and erasing the stigmas the dancers faced.

00:02:38.328 --> 00:02:40.745
(soft music)

